    "body": "Closes #62866\n\n### What this does\nThe MooncakeStoreConnector documentation doesn't mention `kv_load_failure_policy`. When running Mooncake as a shared prefix cache (or with single-node disk offloading), the default `\"fail\"` policy can cause requests to terminate silently with an empty response if a store node drops or a disk read times out.\n\nThis PR adds documentation for `kv_load_failure_policy` and provides an example using `\"recompute\"` so vLLM recovers by computing missing blocks locally. It also adds a quick note clarifying that `MC_RPC_*` timeout variables are read by Mooncake rather than vLLM.\n\n### Motivation & Scope\nI kept this change minimal (+19 lines) and placed it directly under `## KV Transfer Config` where users look for `--kv-transfer-config` options, keeping everything in one place without duplicating notes.\n\n### Testing\n- Verified markdown rendering and header hierarchy.\n- Checked CLI syntax for `--kv-transfer-config`.\n\n*(Prepared with AI assistance and manually reviewed by me)*",
